  "details": "Hi considering there are paramaters for looking left/right\n\nHow fast the player is moving and falling\n\netc\n\nI think it'd be beneficial, either client side or in SDK \n\n(SDK would probably be more beneficial for control and Quest compatiblity)\n\nBake how for example hair moves to 6 or so animations (without gravity)\n\nSo that players hair/ears/tail etc could still be flowy and lively at a distance but with less of a performance cost than calculating it in realtime\n\nObviously this'd miss out on being interactive but I think as something to configure in safety settings (Like show physics for Known but User just has animated fake physics)\n\nAnd or in Avatar culling, like within 3m avatars have full physics but past that it's animated\n\nCould potentially be really nice\n\nAnd in the SDK it'd be especially nice for long hair with Quest compatible avatars\n\nAs you could set it up with way more bones than Quest can do physics for and then just animate it (maybe use constraints, or a chain of 2-3? bones to do Gravity)",
